Subject: [PATCH] AROS host: WordCraft in an Intuition window through egui-aros

apps/wordcraft-aros runs the egui interface with egui-aros: winit and egui-winit for the window and input, the CPU renderer or OpenGL chosen at run time (--gui-renderer, ToolType GUI_RENDERER, the GUI_RENDERER variable; AUTO by default, which closes a software rasterizer's context and draws with the CPU), ASL requesters, and the system clipboard for text (system character set, UTF-8 under CSET 106) and pictures (datatypes; Paste inserts them through the existing clipboard_picture service). It follows the desktop app's start-up: preferences, user fonts and dictionary, recovery, the Start screen, document names from the Shell or Workbench resolved by DOS. Settings, the log and recovery data live in WordCraftData beside the program (WORDCRAFT_PROFILE_DIR). The program runs in the -nix path mode; requesters' DOS names are converted at the edge. The Cargo.lock entries for egui-aros come from the build (scripts/craft.py), as for the other Craft ports.
